[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m zero-length string with a neighbour buffer filled to all 99 usable bytes so that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m any spill would change the printed number.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 7. `printf("%zu\n", ...)` formatting and stream usage
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Plain decimal, no padding or precision, exactly one trailing newline, on stdout
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only. The C never writes to stderr and always returns 0, including on empty
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m input — there is no error path in this program, so "exit status matches" means
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "both exit 0 on everything". Asserted explicitly in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `output_is_a_decimal_number_and_one_trailing_newline_on_stdout_only`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 8. Bytes that are not valid UTF-8
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C is byte-oriented throughout. The Rust operates on `[u8; 100]` and never
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m converts to `str`, so no lossy replacement or panic can occur. Covered by tests
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m over bytes `0xff 0xfe 0xfd`, Latin-1 input, and byte ranges 1..=90 and 150..=240.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Coverage of the enumerated input classes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every branch point in the C is one row here. All 37 tests assert stdout, stderr
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and exit status together.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | input class | test | prints |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | empty input, both `fgets` return NULL | `empty_input_both_fgets_return_null` | `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `"\n"` only, second `fgets` returns NULL | `only_a_newline_second_fgets_returns_null` | `0` |
